{"agent":"bugfix2","data":{"by":"bugfix2","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The patch only changes the unavailable reason text; it does not make the kept worktree runnable. When `ddflow merge --keep` leaves the worktree present at the merge commit (the reported “tree present at 9cc3ba6ca”), `_where_to_run` still returns `cwd is None`, so `ddflow/api/gates/_run.py:316-318` still records UNAVAILABLE. The new `_kept_tree` checks only `path.is_dir()` and never checks the worktree’s HEAD or dirtiness, yet the new `disposition` unconditionally says the tree “does not stand at the merged tree (it was moved or dirtied off the merge)”. That is a new false claim on this input, and the command still pushes the user to hand-record with `gate record --outcome passed`, so B-gate-run-after-keep-merge is not actually fixed.","digest":"fe1684575f76e3cd","location":"ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_no_tree_reason","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_no_tree_reason"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"61efff7741ee04b9","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-gate-run-after-keep-merge.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261105T210018Z-250fdaff.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"cf8f031ff43a+clean"},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 1 chunk(s) were reviewed (1); those findings are checkpointed, the remaining chunks were not reviewed, which is not a pass"},"id":"ecc7698b1ce29d5f46a2dffa4","kind":"gate.partial","lamport":143083,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-gate-run-after-keep-merge","ts":"2026-11-05T21:10:09.659407Z"}
