{"agent":"bugfix2","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The helper decides that a merge kept the worktree by looking only at the current filesystem state: `if not it.worktree` and `path.is_dir()`. It never inspects the recorded merge outcome such as the response’s `worktree_removed=false`. Therefore, if `ddflow merge --keep` keeps the tree, but the kept path is deleted later—for example a cleanup/`remove_on_merge` equivalent or a manual removal occurs before `ddflow gate run DX-fleet-registry unit_tests`—`_kept_tree` returns `None`, and `_no_tree_reason` emits exactly the false message this change is supposed to eliminate: \"the merge removed its worktree\". The merge did not remove it; the later deletion did, so the bug remains for that interleaving. The fix should use persistent merge metadata, not the transient existence of the directory.","digest":"fee230c67a7090f8","location":"ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_kept_tree","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_kept_tree"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_kept_tree` only checks that the worktree directory still exists, and every `merged_sha` path then states that tree \"does not stand at the merged tree\" without comparing it to `it.merged_sha`. After a fast-forward `merge --keep` (or `remove_on_merge=false`) the kept checkout is exactly the merged commit, yet `gate run` still records UNAVAILABLE and prints that false disposition, and still tells the agent to `gate record ... --outcome passed`. The new test only covers a merge-commit plus a later main commit, so it never hits this input.","digest":"4da12e9995458745","location":"ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_kept_tree","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_kept_tree"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":7139,"diff_sha":"e153d8452276b4f1c59ace9fc43f042c7baf1cd73a0bce3d584383d62e39fe98","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":512.8,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"7eafb365383e4078","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-gate-run-after-keep-merge.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261105T211546Z-696fb5fd.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"357e7896e0e401e024cc09109719eff736b7e9df","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/gates/_run.py":"100644 0fe1eb5a1b0d809689212b44ff32f3e90a611f33","ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py":"100644 58b4506e4b318512380702df5c044964d3cbe919","tests/test_gate_run_after_merge.py":"100644 f8b374a2d0025619688746b6c88da5d6f003505b"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","reviewer_families":["deepseek","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_kept_tree","ddflow/api/gates/_tree.py:_kept_tree"],"tree_sha":"357e7896e0e4+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"eb95a7bb88f73f2db44842c1c","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":143208,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-gate-run-after-keep-merge","ts":"2026-11-05T21:24:51.656971Z"}
